Don't worry, yours could very well be the only "legit" use of save
scumming, really; I'd suggest you to read some spoilers about Master
Kaen; he hits really, really hard (claw physical 16d2 + claw physical
16d2 + spellcasting clerical + claw steal 1d4; only the physical part
averages 50.5 damage each action, and he's as fast as you - especially
if he casts haste) and it's really a bad idea to fight him directly -
especially given the usual Monk's bad AC.

Either use a wand (or the spell) of sleep and beat him as hard as you
can, or make a boulder fort around the upstairs with a scroll of earth
- then use ranged attacks: shurikens are probably the best, but even
enough rocks are enough, really. Make a permanent Elbereth to deal
with Xorns and giants (and kill the latter as soon as you can - they
can pick up your boulders).



